es-menu: openSystemEmulatorSettings saves to SystemConf, not Settings

SystemData::getEmulator()/getCore() read the per-system emulator/core from
SystemConf on non-Windows builds (Settings only on WIN32), and the canonical
popSystemConfigurationGui path saves to SystemConf. But
openSystemEmulatorSettings's save func always wrote to Settings, so on Linux
the chosen emulator/core landed in a file nothing reads and the game still
launched with the default. Mirror the same WIN32/else split as the readers.

--- a/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp
@@ -4044,8 +4044,16 @@
 
 	s->addSaveFunc([system, emul_choice, core_choice]
 	{
+#if WIN32 && !_DEBUG
 		Settings::getInstance()->setString(system->getName() + ".emulator", emul_choice->getSelected());
 		Settings::getInstance()->setString(system->getName() + ".core", core_choice->getSelected());
+#else
+		// SystemData::getEmulator()/getCore() read these from SystemConf on
+		// non-Windows builds, so the save has to target SystemConf too or the
+		// per-system emulator/core choice is written where nothing reads it.
+		SystemConf::getInstance()->set(system->getName() + ".emulator", emul_choice->getSelected());
+		SystemConf::getInstance()->set(system->getName() + ".core", core_choice->getSelected());
+#endif
 	});
 
 	mWindow->pushGui(s);
